255: return your best guess of each player's batting handedness and
256: bowling style based on your prior knowledge of the player.
257: 
258: For EVERY player (both playing XI and bench, both teams) return:
259:   "batting_style":  "RHB"  (right-hand batsman)
260:                   | "LHB"  (left-hand batsman)
261:                   | "unknown"  (you genuinely don't know)
262:   "bowling_style":  a short English phrase like
263:                     "Right-arm fast"
264:                     "Right-arm medium-fast"
265:                     "Right-arm medium"
266:                     "Right-arm off-spin"
267:                     "Right-arm legbreak"
268:                     "Right-arm legbreak googly"
269:                     "Left-arm fast"
270:                     "Left-arm medium"
271:                     "Slow left-arm orthodox"
272:                     "Left-arm wrist-spin (chinaman)"
273:                   | "None"  (the player does not bowl at all)
274:                   | "unknown" (you don't know)
275: 
276: "unknown" is ALWAYS acceptable and preferred over a confident wrong
277: guess.  Do not make up styles you are not sure of — the next stage
278: of the pipeline will look up uncertain answers on the web.
279: 
280: Return ONLY a single JSON object keyed by the player's full name
281: EXACTLY as given below (spelling, spacing, punctuation, accents all
282: preserved).  Every player must appear as a key.  No extra keys, no
283: markdown fences, no explanation.
284: 
285: Example shape:
286: {
287:   "Rovman Powell":  {"batting_style": "RHB", "bowling_style": "Right-arm medium"},
288:   "Gudakesh Motie": {"batting_style": "LHB", "bowling_style": "Slow left-arm orthodox"},
289:   "Phil Salt":      {"batting_style": "RHB", "bowling_style": "None"}
290: }
