2336:         # stale strip lingering for a couple of seconds after over
2337:         # rollover.  Reject the identity flip (we still drop through
2338:         # below only if the current_bowler already matches — updating
2339:         # the SAME bowler's stats mid-spell is fine).
2340:         #
2341:         # `_prev_over_bowler` stays pinned until the NEXT over change
2342:         # replaces it, so this rule keeps protecting the current over
2343:         # for its entire duration — not just the first N frames.
2344:         #
2345:         # Reject ALL updates (both identity and figures) when the
2346:         # incoming name matches the previous-over bowler.  If the read
2347:         # is wrong about the name, the figures attached to that read
2348:         # are also wrong (Scout is looking at the wrong graphic) and
2349:         # would otherwise poison the previous bowler's career totals.
2350:         _cur_now = self._inn.get("current_bowler") if self._inn else None
2351:         if (self._prev_over_bowler
2352:                 and name == self._prev_over_bowler):
2353:             # Fix #3 (2026-04-23): recoverable override.
2354:             # Our _prev_over_bowler record is a best-effort snapshot
2355:             # taken at over-rollover.  If Scout consistently disagrees
2356:             # — reading the same "forbidden" name across multiple
2357:             # frames — the odds are our record is wrong (mis-labelled
2358:             # over boundary, cold-start rotation, mid-match restart
2359:             # without full context).  After N consistent rejections,
2360:             # flip: accept the read and clear the lockout.  Observed
2361:             # failure this guard recovers from: MI vs CSK 2026-04-23,
2362:             # F12-F27 stuck with current_bowler=None because rotation
