2399:         # Two defense branches, split by identity-vs-current:
2400:         #
2401:         # IDENTITY CHANGE (name != current):
2402:         #   (a) Same-figures stale graphic — incoming name brings
2403:         #       the exact figures already recorded for them, no new
2404:         #       info, just the same graphic re-read. Rejected
2405:         #       OUTSIDE must_change grace (inside grace a returning
2406:         #       bowler legitimately shows last-spell figures).
2407:         #   Regression check DOES NOT apply on identity change:
2408:         #   different bowlers have independent spells, so comparing
2409:         #   an incoming bowler's proposed overs to their own
2410:         #   previously-recorded figures would wrongly block a
2411:         #   legitimate handover read whenever the incoming bowler's
2412:         #   last recorded value happens to be corrupt-high.  That
2413:         #   class of bug is handled by the SAME-identity branch
2414:         #   below with recoverable override.
2415:         #
2416:         # SAME IDENTITY (name == current):
2417:         #   (b) Overs-regression with recoverable override — a real
2418:         #       spell only goes forward, so lower overs means stale
2419:         #       cache OR corrupted lock. We reject the first few
2420:         #       regression reads; if the same lower proposal
2421:         #       persists for `_BOWLER_REGRESS_OVERRIDE_N` frames,
2422:         #       the recorded value is the corrupt one and we allow
2423:         #       the override (log loudly — this is the unstick path
2424:         #       for phantom high-water records).
