   2: 
   3: Every test corresponds to a specific fix the user asked for. The tests
   4: are intentionally small, side-effect free, and use only the in-memory
   5: state of the relevant module — no Scout, no video, no WebSocket. They
   6: exist purely to confirm the protective logic is wired in and behaves
   7: the way the fix advertises.
   8: 
   9: Run from the project root:
  10: 
  11:     cd files && .venv/bin/python test_recent_fixes.py
  12: 
  13: Each test prints PASS/FAIL with a short description. Process exits 0
  14: if every test passes, 1 otherwise.
